.terraform
keys/
.env
# The bare pattern above only catches a literal `.env` — `apps/caddy/.env` is
# covered by it, but a differently-named env file anywhere under apps/ (or a
# `.env.local`) would not be. There is no secret scanner in this repo's CI, and
# main is force-mirrored to a public repo on every push, so cover the whole
# apps/ tree explicitly rather than relying on the root pattern reaching it.
apps/**/*.env
!apps/**/*.env.example
*.tfvars
# ...except the fleet map, which is the authoring surface for compute instances
# and is read by both compute/vm and infra/storage via _terraform.yml's
# var_file input. Non-secret values only: main is force-mirrored to a public repo.
!fleet.tfvars
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
.idea/
*.tfplan
tfplan
crash.log
